SUMMARY:Meet the Maker: Jefferson's Bourbon | Session II 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 1 spot le
 ft\nStatus: You are on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.c
 om/events/206917\n\nJoin us for an intimate tasting experience with Jeffer
 son’s Bourbon\, exploring the craftsmanship\, character\, and creativity
  behind each pour. The evening begins with a welcome cocktail and time to 
 mingle before a guided tasting led by Jefferson’s founder Trey Zoeller. 
 A Kentucky native with deep family ties to American whiskey\, Zoeller foun
 ded Jefferson’s with his father in 1997 and has become known for challen
 ging bourbon tradition through inventive approaches to aging and blending\
 , earning him a place in the Kentucky Bourbon Hall of Fame.\n\nAs straight
  tasting pours are passed\, Trey will share the story of Jefferson’s whi
 le guiding members through the flavor profiles\, production process\, and 
 distinctive character of each selection. Following the tasting\, the eveni
 ng opens back up for conversation\, giving members the opportunity to ming
 le\, revisit their favorites\, and connect with Trey one-on-one for questi
 ons and a deeper dive into the world of Jefferson’s Bourbon.\n\n*This ev
 ent is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bi
 tes and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations 
 be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206917
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-206949@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261030T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T190000
SUMMARY:Trials and Truth: A History of Witchcraft
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 34 spots lef
 t\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/
 events/206949\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion\n\nIn a seasonal ode
  to witchcraft\, join us for a thought provoking exploration tracing the m
 yths\, origins\, and histories that have shaped its place in a Western Eur
 opean cultural lineage\, a lineage that runs through to the Americas and i
 nto the present day. Building on last year's Trials & Truth\, which examin
 ed the Salem Witch Trials\, Professor Julie Walsh returns to take the conv
 ersation beyond local lore\, exploring the European roots of the image of 
 the witch\, its enduring stereotypes\, and the complex relationship betwee
 n belief\, skepticism\, and the social consequences of believing the worst
  about your neighbors. The evening will delve into the origin story of th
 e medieval witch\, what this story reveals about power\, fear\, freedom\, 
 and social justice. \n\nJulie Walsh is the Whitehead Associate Professor 
 of Critical Thought\, Associate Professor of Philosophy\, and Director of 
 the Newhouse Center for the Humanities at the Wellesley College\; she spec
 ializes in early modern philosophy\, theories of freedom\, and the history
  of witchcraft. She will be in conversation with Liza Oliver\, Associate P
 rofessor of Art History and Director of the Pluralism Initiative at Welle
 sley College\; she specializes in the intersections of art\, colonialism\,
  and cultural history. Together\, they will offer members a fresh perspect
 ive on the historical roots and ongoing social impact of European ideas of
  witches\, witchcraft\, and evil. \n\n*This event is complimentary and re
 served for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will b
 e served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours p
 rior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206949
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208796@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261102T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261102T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261102T183000
SUMMARY:Behind Broadway: A Performance with Lorna Courtney 
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: $50.00 per person\nAvailability: 48 
 spots left\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinh
 ouse.com/events/208796\n\n5:00PM Doors Open\, 5:15PM Performance\, 6:00PM 
 Reception\nJoin us in The Reading Room for an intimate evening of music\, 
 theatre\, and storytelling with Tony Award-nominated Broadway star Lorna C
 ourtney. Best known for originating the role of Juliet in the hit musical 
 “& Juliet”\, Courtney brings her extraordinary talent to The ’Quin f
 or a captivating live performance featuring selections from across her car
 eer\, from her early days on Broadway to her celebrated roles in “Heathe
 rs: The Musical” and “The Rocky Horror Picture Show”. Through song a
 nd personal storytelling\, Courtney will take members on a journey through
  the defining performances\, inspirations\, and experiences that have shap
 ed her career on the stage.\n\nFollowing the 30 minute performance\, Court
 ney will be joined for an engaging conversation and Q&A with Artistic Dire
 ctor of SpeakEasy Stage Company\, Dawn Simmons. Together\, the two will of
 fer a behind-the-curtain look at the world of Broadway\, exploring the cre
 ative process\, pivotal career moments\, and the evolving landscape of mus
 ical theatre while members enjoy light bites.\n\n*Tickets are $50 per mem
 ber and $75 for one registered guest. All tickets are nonrefundable and no
 ntransferable. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/208796
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
